      "source": "hackernews",
      "title": "The Spray Bottle",
      "url": "https://mechanical-pencil.com/products/spray-bottle",
      "score": 586,
      "comments": 141,
      "hn_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50598555",
      "published_at": "2026-11-22T11:16:30+00:00",
      "full_text": "Why the Spray Bottle?\nNOV 2026\nWhen I first started designing this site, I would constantly look around my home for objects that I had never given a second thought. Two products stood out to me as wonderfully mechanical and common: the mechanical pencil and the spray bottle.\nThe modern spray bottle emerged in the early 1970s, and by now there must be hundreds, maybe even thousands, of spray bottle designs out there in the world, with variations on their nozzle design, trigger mechanism and more. But they all utilize the same basic one-way-valve mechanism.\nThe main question we want to answer: How does fluid keep spraying out, pull after pull, every time you squeeze the Trigger? Let's get into it!\nHow Do You Use A Spray Bottle?\nBefore we look inside, let’s cover the basics: pull the Trigger to spray, release it to reload.\nWhat's Inside a Spray Bottle?\nLet’s take the Spray Bottle apart to see what’s inside\nLet's Look At The Moving Parts\nClick through to see how the moving parts connect\nLet's Break Down the One-Way Valve\nA one-way valve is exactly what it sounds like: a valve that lets fluid flow one way and blocks it from going the other way. They are everywhere. Soap bottles, toilets, even your heart! Let's examine how it works in the context of the Spray Bottle.\nLet's Step Through the Mechanism\nClick through the spray mechanism to see how all the parts work together.",
